## Error Handling with Timeouts

### Graceful Timeout Handling
```bash
# Use timeout with error handling
if timeout 30 python3 nodes/lora.py; then
    echo "LoRa node started successfully"
else
    exit_code=$?
    if [ $exit_code -eq 124 ]; then
        echo "LoRa node startup timed out"
    else
        echo "LoRa node failed with exit code $exit_code"
    fi
fi
```

### Timeout with Cleanup
```bash
# Start process with timeout and cleanup
timeout 60 python3 nodes/lora.py &
LORA_PID=$!

# Cleanup function
cleanup() {
    if kill -0 $LORA_PID 2>/dev/null; then
        kill $LORA_PID
        echo "Cleaned up LoRa process"
    fi
}

# Set trap for cleanup
trap cleanup EXIT
```

